# Material Design 3: Core Tokens and Foundations

This project uses Material Design 3 as its design language. Use the official `@material/web` token names so custom components and `<md-*>` components theme together. Never hardcode hex colors, radii, font sizes, or shadows in components; always reference a token.

Companion rules: `m3-components.mdc` (components) and `m3-layout-motion-a11y.mdc` (layout, motion, accessibility, content).

## Token hierarchy
Reference tokens (concrete values) -> System tokens (roles/decisions) -> Component tokens (per-component overrides).
- Reference: `--md-ref-typeface-brand`, `--md-ref-typeface-plain`
- System: `--md-sys-color-*`, `--md-sys-typescale-*`, `--md-sys-shape-corner-*`
- Component: e.g. `--md-filled-button-container-shape` (component tokens are NOT prefixed with `comp`)
- Tokens are CSS custom properties and can be scoped with any selector. Prefer changing system tokens globally; use component tokens only for deliberate one-off variants.

## Color
Every role has a matching `on-` role for content placed on it. Pair them; never mix (e.g. don't put `on-surface` text on `primary` backgrounds).

Roles: `primary`, `secondary`, `tertiary`, `error` (each with `-container`), `background`, `surface`, `surface-dim`, `surface-bright`, `surface-container-lowest|low|(none)|high|highest`, `surface-variant`, `outline`, `outline-variant`, `inverse-surface`, `inverse-on-surface`, `inverse-primary`, `surface-tint`, `shadow`, `scrim`.

Baseline scheme (replace with a scheme generated from the brand seed color using Material Theme Builder or `@material/material-color-utilities`):
```css
:root {
  --md-sys-color-primary: #6750A4;           --md-sys-color-on-primary: #FFFFFF;
  --md-sys-color-primary-container: #EADDFF; --md-sys-color-on-primary-container: #21005D;
  --md-sys-color-secondary: #625B71;         --md-sys-color-on-secondary: #FFFFFF;
  --md-sys-color-secondary-container: #E8DEF8; --md-sys-color-on-secondary-container: #1D192B;
  --md-sys-color-tertiary: #7D5260;          --md-sys-color-on-tertiary: #FFFFFF;
  --md-sys-color-tertiary-container: #FFD8E4; --md-sys-color-on-tertiary-container: #31111D;
  --md-sys-color-error: #B3261E;             --md-sys-color-on-error: #FFFFFF;
  --md-sys-color-error-container: #F9DEDC;   --md-sys-color-on-error-container: #410E0B;
  --md-sys-color-background: #FEF7FF;        --md-sys-color-on-background: #1D1B20;
  --md-sys-color-surface: #FEF7FF;           --md-sys-color-on-surface: #1D1B20;
  --md-sys-color-surface-variant: #E7E0EC;   --md-sys-color-on-surface-variant: #49454F;
  --md-sys-color-surface-dim: #DED8E1;       --md-sys-color-surface-bright: #FEF7FF;
  --md-sys-color-surface-container-lowest: #FFFFFF;
  --md-sys-color-surface-container-low: #F7F2FA;
  --md-sys-color-surface-container: #F3EDF7;
  --md-sys-color-surface-container-high: #ECE6F0;
  --md-sys-color-surface-container-highest: #E6E0E9;
  --md-sys-color-outline: #79747E;           --md-sys-color-outline-variant: #CAC4D0;
  --md-sys-color-inverse-surface: #322F35;   --md-sys-color-inverse-on-surface: #F5EFF7;
  --md-sys-color-inverse-primary: #D0BCFF;   --md-sys-color-surface-tint: #6750A4;
  --md-sys-color-shadow: #000000;            --md-sys-color-scrim: #000000;
}
/* Dark: material-web does not switch schemes automatically. Override the same tokens. */
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root:not([data-theme="light"]) { /* ...dark tokens below... */ }
}
:root[data-theme="dark"] { /* ...dark tokens below... */ }
```
