### Color usage rules
- Page background: `surface` (or `background`). Grouped content: `surface-container-*` (lower = recessed, higher = raised).
- Body text: `on-surface`. Secondary text and icons: `on-surface-variant`. Disabled: `on-surface` at 38%.
- Borders/dividers: `outline` (strong, e.g. outlined buttons/fields), `outline-variant` (subtle, e.g. dividers, card outlines).
- Emphasis ladder for actions: filled `primary` (one per area) > filled tonal `secondary-container` > outlined > text.
- `tertiary` is for contrasting accents that balance primary (badges, highlights), not a third brand color for everything.
- `error` only for errors/destructive states. Never use color alone to convey meaning; add icon or text.
- Dynamic color: when theming from a user/brand seed, regenerate the entire scheme (light + dark); don't tweak single roles by hand.

## Typography
Load fonts: default is Roboto 400/500/700. If you change typeface, load all three weights.
```css
:root {
  --md-ref-typeface-brand: 'Roboto';   /* headings: display, headline, title */
  --md-ref-typeface-plain: 'Roboto';   /* body, label */
}
```
Apply type with `.md-typescale-<scale>-<size>` classes (import `@material/web/typography/md-typescale-styles.js` and add `typescaleStyles.styleSheet` to `document.adoptedStyleSheets`), or with tokens: `--md-sys-typescale-<scale>-<size>-(font|size|line-height|weight)`. Scales: display, headline, title, body, label; sizes: small, medium, large.

| Style | Size / line-height | Weight | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| display-large / medium / small | 57/64, 45/52, 36/44 | 400 | Hero numbers, short expressive text |
| headline-large / medium / small | 32/40, 28/36, 24/32 | 400 | Page and section headings |
| title-large | 22/28 | 400 | App bar title, dialog headline |
| title-medium / small | 16/24, 14/20 | 500 | Card titles, list headlines, tabs |
| body-large / medium / small | 16/24, 14/20, 12/16 | 400 | Paragraphs, supporting text |
| label-large / medium / small | 14/20, 12/16, 11/16 | 500 | Buttons, chips, captions, nav labels |

Rules: sentence case everywhere (no ALL CAPS buttons); max line length ~60-75ch for body; use heading level semantics (`h1`-`h6`) independently of typescale class; don't invent sizes outside this scale.

## Shape
```css
:root {
  --md-sys-shape-corner-none: 0px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-extra-small: 4px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-small: 8px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-medium: 12px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-large: 16px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-extra-large: 28px;
  --md-sys-shape-corner-full: 9999px;
}
```
Guide: buttons, chips-as-pills, switches, search = full; chips = small; cards = medium; FAB = large; dialogs, bottom sheets (top corners), navigation drawer = extra-large; text field container (filled) = extra-small top corners; images in cards = medium; badges = full. Nested shapes: inner radius = outer radius minus padding.

## Elevation
In M3, hierarchy comes primarily from tonal surface color; shadows are secondary. Use `<md-elevation>` or these levels:
```css
:root {
  --m3-elev-0: none;
  --m3-elev-1: 0 1px 2px rgb(0 0 0 / .30), 0 1px 3px 1px rgb(0 0 0 / .15);
  --m3-elev-2: 0 1px 2px rgb(0 0 0 / .30), 0 2px 6px 2px rgb(0 0 0 / .15);
  --m3-elev-3: 0 1px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / .30), 0 4px 8px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / .15);
  --m3-elev-4: 0 2px 3px rgb(0 0 0 / .30), 0 6px 10px 4px rgb(0 0 0 / .15);
  --m3-elev-5: 0 4px 4px rgb(0 0 0 / .30), 0 8px 12px 6px rgb(0 0 0 / .15);
}
```
Level 0: page, filled/outlined cards at rest. 1: elevated cards, elevated buttons, nav drawer/rail (modal). 2: menus, nav bar, scrolled app bar. 3: FAB, dialogs, search bar, date picker. 4-5: only for drag/hover emphasis. Pair elevation with `surface-container*` tone, not black overlays.

## State layers (interaction feedback)
Overlay `currentColor`/the on-color on the container: hover 8%, focus 10%, pressed 10%, dragged 16%. Disabled: content 38% opacity, container 12%. Use `<md-ripple>` + `<md-focus-ring>` in custom interactive elements, or an equivalent `::before`/`::after` overlay. Never change a component's base color to indicate hover.

## Token usage rules for generated code
1. Colors: `var(--md-sys-color-*)` only. Radii: `var(--md-sys-shape-corner-*)`. Text: typescale class or tokens.
2. Spacing in multiples of 4px (common: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32, 48).
3. If a needed value has no token, add a documented token to `:root` first (prefix custom ones `--app-*`), then use it.
4. Tailwind projects: map in `theme.extend` (`colors.primary: 'var(--md-sys-color-primary)'`, `colors['on-primary']`, `borderRadius.md: 'var(--md-sys-shape-corner-medium)'`) and use semantic class names, never raw palette classes.
